{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /experiments/circuit/review-notes.md /experiments/circuit/vnl5050-primary-web.txt /experiments/circuit/vnl-reference-web.txt'","aggregated_output":"# Circuit review record\n\nCandidate: 69119fab9d25319b3bf376eca634b13104ba76b7417416b85a2a64a4e78a6ab4\nRun: bafd7961-39b9-4a34-9b39-b7f108e82f07\nPacket SHA256: 7443dc72bd7dc0c25527bd0f1550b7d74a74454d412e30e18634608d420b4731\nReview date: 2026-10-16. Role: circuit.\n\n## Commands and records\n\nRead-only discovery used `rg --files /candidate/project`, `rg --files /evidence/checks`, and targeted `rg -n` / `sed -n` source reads. No AGENTS.md was found in the searched candidate, evidence and workspace paths. Credentials were not read. No prior reviewer experiments were used.\n\nRead all fresh JSON check records and complete ERC/DRC reports under /evidence, including their execution records, excluded violations, ignored rule lists, geometry and native XML netlist. Used Python json/xml parsers to enumerate the reports, component attributes and connectivity. The packet's text truncation was overcome by reading the complete local files.\n\nVersions: `kicad-cli version`, `python3 --version`, `ngspice --version`; results in versions.txt. ngspice was not used for an electrical experiment because neither complete module circuits nor verified device models/stimuli were supplied. No electrical behavior is inferred from successful tool exits.\n\nIndependent export: `kicad-cli sch export netlist --format kicadxml -o /work/experiments/independent-netlist.xml /candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch`; exit 0. Python XML comparison against /evidence/work/netlist/design.xml gave identical pin-net memberships. See connectivity-comparison.json.\n\n`python3 /work/experiments/audit.py > /work/experiments/audit-console.txt`; exit 0. The script reads the native schematic S-expressions and saved PCB through pcbnew without saving. pcbnew printed three PROPERTY_ENUM assertions ('No enum choices defined') on stderr during import; audit output was produced and its board hash equals the check record. This was not treated as electrical evidence or as a candidate circuit defect. audit.json records 10 sheet instances, 139 components, 199 nets, identical alias bytes, zero schematic-to-native-pad net-name mismatches and selected board pad assignments. This validates identities, not geometric continuity; saved-zone physical checks remain those in the fresh DRC record.\n\n`python3 /work/experiments/calculations.py > /work/experiments/calculations-console.txt`; static bounds only. No scratch candidate edit or proposed fix was tested.\n\n## Primary references and source retrieval\n\nPython urllib.request fetched references, followed by `pdftotext -layout <pdf> <txt>`. URLs, outcomes and failures are in retrieval.json, retrieval-extra.json and retrieval-vnl5050.json. Native candidate remained read-only throughout.\n\n- NXP TJA1051, https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/TJA1051.pdf : local tja1051.pdf / tja1051.txt. Table 3 pin definitions; normal/silent mode; VCC 4.5–5.5 V and VIO 2.8–5.5 V operating ranges; Table 7 differential input resistance 19/30/52 kohm. Native U20/U21 use 5 V VCC, 3.3 V VIO, S grounded, correct pin numbers, independent TXD/RXD pairs and common CAN2 bus. These supply names are nominal values; no rail tolerance/transient verification was provided.\n- Infineon TLE9201SG, https://www.infineon.com/assets/row/public/documents/10/49/infineon-tle9201sg-ds-en.pdf : local tle9201.pdf / tle9201.txt. Pin Configuration and Electrical Characteristics confirm VSO may be 3.3 V and DIS/CSN have pull-up currents. The native unconnected SPI inputs are not assumed to prevent direct DIR/PWM/DIS operation. Native 10 kohm DIS pulls go to 3.3 V. No shutdown/brownout waveform or firmware reset timing was verified.\n- TI DRV8825, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/drv8825.pdf : local drv8825.pdf / drv8825.txt. Logic high minimum 2.2 V. Native A1 control wiring has 5 V reset/sleep, grounded enable/mode pins, and LS9/10 STEP/DIR. The high-Z 2.5 V nominal divider alone is not proof of a failed STEP/DIR input.\n- ST VNL5090N3-E/VNL5090S5-E, https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/vnl5090n3-e.pdf : direct urllib retrieval timed out; web extraction is retained in vnl-reference-web.txt. Table 6: N3 operating control supply minimum 3.5 V. Table 8: N3 input threshold up to 3.5 V. N3 input is also its supply. S5's separate logic-input limit must not be substituted for N3's rating.\n- ST VNL5050N3-E/VNL5050S5-E, https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/vnl5050s5-e.pdf : web extraction retained in vnl5050-primary-web.txt; Table 6 and Table 8 have the same 3.5 V supply minimum / threshold maximum relevant to this review. This PDF covers both N3 and S5; only the N3 rows apply to the native SOT-223. Direct retrieval of the N3 URL timed out; a distributor PDF fetch returned HTTP 403. These retrieval failures are not native rule failures.\n- LCSC SKU identity source, https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2680415.html : vnl-reference-web.txt retains the web result identifying MPN VNL5050N3TR-E, SKU C2680415 and SOT-223. LCSC is used as the primary authority for its own stock code, not as the authority for electrical limits. Native U11–U14/U16–U19 specify Value VNL5090 and the conflicting SKU; the same discrepancy exists on the saved board. No declared alternate-part qualification was located. This is an identity inconsistency, not proof of a pinout failure or an overload.\n- Polygonus maintainer README, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FOME-Tech/Polygonus/master/README.md : local polygonus-readme.md, fetched as external reference, not candidate native source. Outputs section and pinout identify LS9–12 / IGN9–12 as MCU passthrough and distinguish IGN1–8 as 5 V push-pull. Exact module hardware revision / MCU supply circuit is not in this candidate; the 3.3 V lowside drive assessment is therefore conditional and reported as a concern. No external module source was substituted for the reviewed donor.\n- Analog Devices MAX9924–MAX9927, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924-MAX9927.pdf : web text inspected for supply, pin numbering, mode A1 and output pull-up. Direct download timed out. Native U10 uses named 5 V supply, an approximately 2.5 V external bias divider and output pull-up to 3.3 V; no input amplitude/frequency sweep or model was run. Physical sensor polarity is not inferred from labels alone.\n\n## Findings basis and rejected overclaims\n\nCAN2: native wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch resistor UUID d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543 has value 120, DNP yes, excluded from BOM. Its two sheet instances are R36 and R37. Both native board footprints also have DNP attributes and pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-. No populated direct resistor across these two nets exists on the carrier. The two transceiver input resistances are not replacements for termination. J2.73/74 and J1.15/11 expose the bus to unknown module/harness termination; absence of a documented complete termination configuration is a concern, not a demonstrated CAN failure. No bus rate, topology impedance, transmitted waveform, receiver sampling measurement or passive DC resistance measurement was supplied.\n\nLowside drive: all eight VNL SOT-223 inputs are fed from GPIO interface nets via 1 kohm RN2/RN4 branches, with 1 kohm RN1/RN3 pulls to ground at the GPIO nets. There is no 5 V buffer. LS9/10 additionally have native 1 kohm pulls to 5 V, yielding 2.5 V unloaded when GPIOs float. For a 3.3 V push-pull GPIO, the driver input is at most 3.3 V before series-resistor drop. Both possible N3 part identities specify 3.5 V minimum control supply. This shows missing guaranteed drive margin under that conditional module configuration; it does not establish that all samples fail or quantify load current. At reset the nonzero LS9/10 bias likewise has no demonstrated safe-off waveform. These uncertainties are retained in the concern.\n\nU11–U19 pad 2 no-connect is not treated as an open drain output: each SOT-223 tab pad 4 is assigned the output net. U7's cached library identifier is LM393 but its value and SKU identify MAX9142; no LM393 open-collector model was assumed in assessing its push-pull comparator circuit. U5 NOR latch cross-coupling and grounded unused inputs were traced without asserting power-on latch state.\n\nThe five ERC errors were inspected: three un-driven power-input modeling reports (external ground/VMOT/ignition supplies), one missing explicit FLT no-connect intent, and two identically named module sensor-power output pins tied together. These are native ERC violations; they do not by themselves demonstrate missing physical supply or two independent regulators shorted. No circuit-blocking allegation is made from them. DRC's 13 error-level entries are marked excluded (three incomplete thermal reliefs and five connector mechanical holes each producing padstack/annular reports); no electrical open is inferred from them. The zero-unconnected result is not a waveform or circuit-function measurement.\n\n## Coverage omissions\n\nNo bench measurements, firmware execution, complete-module verification, verified SPICE models, dynamic startup/shutdown/reset/brownout tests, sensor waveform range sweep, CAN arbitration/signal-integrity test or thermal/load qualification. No exact Polygonus/Atlas/wideband module revision is supplied. No module population state or harness termination is established. No automotive transient, ignition-energy, wideband-loop stability, EMC, manufacturing or integrated FOME-MC approval. Saved copper was not refilled or modified. Original as-received checkout is outside this disposable alias candidate review. Component part identity spot checks do not constitute an exhaustive BOM/rating/footprint qualification.\nOMNIFET III fully protected low-side driver (https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet