| cite415†Integrated Circuits (ICs)/Power Management (PMIC)/Power Distribution Switches, Load Drivers | [Input]\nL1238: Manufacturer  | cite561†ST | [Input]\nL1239: Packaging  | SOT-223  | [Input]\nL1240: Operating Temperature  | -40℃~+150℃  | [Input]\nL1241: Features  | Overcurrent Protection;Short-Circuit Protection;Over temperature protection;Overvoltage protection  | [Input]\nL1242: number of channels  | 1  | [Input]\nL1243: Control Input Logic  | Active High  | [Input]\nL1244: Maximum Continuous Current  | 19A  | [Input]\nL1245: RDS(on)  | 50mΩ  | [Input]\nL1246: Operating Voltage  | 3.5V~5.5V  | [Input]\nL1247: Type  | Low Side Switch  | [Input]\nL1248: Type  | Description  |\nL1249: --- | --- | ---\nL1250: Category  | cite415†Integrated Circuits (ICs)/Power Management (PMIC)/Power Distribution Switches, Load Drivers | [Input]\nL1251: Manufacturer  | cite561†ST | [Input]\nL1252: Packaging  | SOT-223  | [Input]\nL1253: Operating Temperature  | -40℃~+150℃  | [Input]\nL1254: Features  | Overcurrent Protection;Short-Circuit Protection;Over temperature protection;Overvoltage protection  | [Input]\nL1255: number of channels  | 1  | [Input]\nL1256: Type  | Description  |\nL1257: --- | --- | ---\nL1258: Control Input Logic  | Active High  | [Input]\nL1259: Maximum Continuous Current  | 19A  | [Input]\nL1260: RDS(on)  | 50mΩ  | [Input]\nL1261: Operating Voltage  | 3.5V~5.5V  | [Input]\nL1262: Type  | Low Side Switch  | [Input]\nL1263: \nL1264: Help & Feedbackcite415†Show similar products (0) > L1265: ## Introduction\nL1266: \nL1267: AI Translation\nL1268: The VNL5050N3-E and VNL5050S5-E are monolithic devices made using VIPower Technology, intended for driving resistive or inductive loads with one side connected to the battery. Built-in thermal shutdown protects the chip from overtemperature and short-circuit. Output current limitation protects the devices in an overload condition. In case of long duration overload, the devices limit the dissipated power to a safe level up to thermal shutdown intervention.\nL1269: Thermal shutdown, with automatic restart, allows the devices to recover normal operation as soon as a fault condition disappears. Fast demagnetization of inductive loads is achieved at turn-off.\nL1270: ## Features\nL1271: \nL1272: AI Translation\nL1273: \nL1274:   * Automotive qualified\nL1275:   * Drain current: 19 A\nL1276:   * ESD protection\nL1277:   * Overvoltage clamp\nL1278:   * Thermal shutdown\nL1279:   * Current and power limitation\nL1280:   * Very low standby current\nL1281:   * Very low electromagnetic susceptibility\nL1282:   * Compliant with European directive 2002/95/EC\nL1283:   * Open drain status output (VNL5050S5-E only)\nL1284: \nL1285: Every Order Guarantee\nL1286: \nL1287: 100% Authentic · 30-Day Return or Replacement\nL1288: \nL1289: Out of Stock\nL1290: \nL1291: Notify Me\nL1292: \nL1293: Minimum: 1 Multiple: 1 Sales Unit: Piece\nL1294: \nL1295: [Input]\nL1296: \nL1297: Add to Cart\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn10view2 [wordlim: 200] Unable to resolve screenshot call because content type is not application/pdf and web screenshot is not enabled\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /experiments/physical/review-notes.md /experiments/circuit/calculations.json /experiments/circuit/polygonus-readme.md; sed -n '1,140p' /experiments/circuit/audit.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /experiments/physical/review-notes.md /experiments/circuit/calculations.json /experiments/circuit/polygonus-readme.md; sed -n '1,140p' /experiments/circuit/audit.py\"","aggregated_output":"# Physical initial review record\n\nCandidate: 69119fab9d25319b3bf376eca634b13104ba76b7417416b85a2a64a4e78a6ab4\nRun: bafd7961-39b9-4a34-9b39-b7f108e82f07\nPacket SHA256: 7443dc72bd7dc0c25527bd0f1550b7d74a74454d412e30e18634608d420b4731\nRole: physical\n\n## Commands and versions\n\n- Reconnaissance: `rg --files` under /candidate/project libraries; read project fp-lib-table, rule_severities, rules, and drc_exclusions in Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pro. Read full /evidence/work/drc/drc.json, erc/erc.json, geometry/geometry.json and netlist/design.xml and connectivity.json using Python JSON/XML parsers. No credential files or other reviewers' experiments read.\n- `python3 /work/experiments/run_checks.py`: commands.json records full argument lists, environment overrides, exit codes and log files. KiCad CLI 10.0.7; Python version is in command-1.log. All exports read the candidate directly and write only experiment artifacts.\n- First independent DRC used a fresh KiCad configuration without a global footprint table. It reproduced the geometric errors, but generated 129 missing-library warnings instead of the supplied report's mix of library mismatch/issues warnings. This is a configuration coverage difference; it is not evidence of a changed board or electrical defect.\n- Repeated DRC after copying only fp-lib-table and sym-lib-table from /evidence/work/drc/kicad-config/10.0 to the experiment configuration. Full command and result are in configured-drc-command.json and configured-drc.log. Result matches supplied report: 142 violations, 114 parity issues, zero unconnected items. All 13 error-level results are excluded. The 13 results are 5 padstack + 5 annular width + 3 starved thermal. KiCad's zero exit code does not mean these checks passed.\n- `/usr/bin/python3 /work/experiments/physical_probe.py > /work/experiments/physical-probe.log 2>&1`: pcbnew 10.0.7 reads saved PCB without refill or save. Source, calculations and assumptions in physical_probe.py; measurements in physical-measurements.json; saved ground copper details in saved-thermal-copper.png. pcbnew startup emits PROPERTY_ENUM assertions; it loads the board and returns measurements. Geometric DRC errors are reproduced by CLI independently of this Python probe.\n- `kicad-cli pcb export drill --excellon-separate-th --generate-report ...` via run_checks.py: drill report and separate PTH/NPTH Excellon outputs are in drill-report.txt and drills/. No copper refill performed.\n- Byte comparison confirmed uppercase sheet alias and lowercase original VR conditioner files are identical in this candidate. This does not adjudicate a separate original checkout.\n\n## Measurements / bounded conclusions\n\n- Board SHA256 4e059d571e0f46911d9101b86c8178298cefb866e2f19d5295a30c35dadedd53 matches supplied checks.\n- Independently exported schematic contains 659 distinct (reference,pin) net assignments. All exist on PCB with identical net names; no extra numbered PCB pins. Repeated copper pads with the same pin number are not separate schematic pins. This check shares the native pin numbering and does not prove a part's pinout is correct.\n- J1's five unnumbered holes are PTH, with pad diameter equal to drill diameter: 3 x 4.0 mm and 2 x 2.2 mm. Radial annulus = (pad diameter - drill diameter)/2 = 0 mm. Native minimum annular width is 0.1 mm. Drill export places all five holes into PTH file, tools T12 and T10, respectively; NPTH file has zero holes. No conclusion made about intended post tolerances or manufacturer acceptance.\n- Ground zone bc540b8b-3ffa-4b00-b211-3a91191a1f6d has saved F.Cu reliefs with one resolved spoke at C15.2, U7.4 and C14.2 where native minimum is two. Each also has a 0.25 mm routed ground connection leading toward a nearby ground via. The defects are native geometric rule violations; no open ground, excess temperature or field failure is established.\n- Both 120 ohm CAN2 shunts R36/R37 are DNP and excluded from BOM and placement on saved PCB and schematic. Both span the same /CAN2+ and /CAN2- nets. They contribute 0 S conductance when absent. Ideal optional population arithmetic: one 120 ohm shunt = 120 ohms; both populated = (1/120 + 1/120)^-1 = 60 ohms. This arithmetic excludes transceiver leakage, protection devices, host-module termination and external harness loads. It is not a waveform simulation.\n- CAN2 routes are about 252.43 mm aggregate track length for CAN2+ and 252.40 mm for CAN2-, each with four vias. Aggregate length includes branches and is not an end-to-end transmission-line length or proof of controlled impedance.\n- Native PCB contains power plane /12V_MR_FUSE and GND zone, and heater-negative routes. Route widths/lengths and via counts recorded to challenge geometry-only conclusions. They do not establish ampacity, ground impedance, allowable heater current, transient behavior or temperature.\n\n## Coverage omissions and limitations\n\nNo zone refill; no hardware resistance or waveform measurement; no CAN traffic, termination sensitivity, bus rate, rise-time, cable or host-module population sweep; no assembled host/wideband module internals established; no 3D connector fit, module standoff clearance, manufacturer drill tolerances or fabrication approval. No component datasheet pinout audit, ignition energy, wideband stability, EMC, automotive transients, thermal simulation, simultaneous output-current/duty-cycle qualification or fuse coordination. No integrated FOME-MC verification. The donor check is not original as-received checkout validation.\n\nERC errors were read but not all adjudicated electrically: external supply flags, a floating fault output, and two power-output-typed sensor supply pins cannot independently establish faulty behavior from ERC alone. Library drift, unavailable custom libraries and largely field-level schematic parity warnings were inspected as coverage limitations, not automatically converted to functional defects. Ignored native checks include missing courtyards and PTH/NPTH inside courtyards; copper-edge minimum is configured as 0 mm. Therefore the check set does not establish mechanical keepouts or an application-specific edge-clearance requirement. No new such requirement was imposed.\n{\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"R_pullup_ohm\": 1000.0,\n    \"R_pulldown_ohm\": 1000.0,\n    \"R_series_ohm\": 1000.0,\n    \"named_5V_rail_V\": 5.0,\n    \"conditional_GPIO_high_V\": 3.3\n  },\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"Native nominal values; no unstated tolerance or temperature corners imposed.\",\n    \"The 3.3 V case is conditional on a Polygonus GPIO powered at 3.3 V; the exact mated module is not in the candidate.\",\n    \"GPIO high-Z case excludes current into U11/U12 and A1; it is the unloaded Thevenin voltage, not a prediction of switch state.\",\n    \"Series resistor cannot raise the downstream input above an ideal voltage-driven source when that input consumes current.\",\n    \"65 uA at 5 V is a published supply-current maximum, not a valid model at 3.3 V; no current extrapolation is used.\"\n  ],\n  \"LS9_LS10_GPIO_highZ\": {\n    \"equation\": \"Vth = 5 * 1000 / (1000 + 1000)\",\n    \"Vth_V\": 2.5,\n    \"Rth_ohm\": 500.0,\n    \"DRV8825_VIH_min_V\": 2.2,\n    \"unloaded_margin_to_DRV8825_VIH_V\": 0.2999999999999998,\n    \"interpretation\": \"Does not prove a failed stepper high. Does leave LS9/10 at a nonzero level with GPIO high-Z; VNL behavior unqualified here.\"\n  },\n  \"lowside_GPIO_3V3_case\": {\n    \"U_input_upper_bound_V\": 3.3,\n    \"N3_operating_supply_min_V\": 3.5,\n    \"upper_bound_minus_operating_min_V\": -0.20000000000000018,\n    \"N3_input_threshold_max_V\": 3.5,\n    \"interpretation\": \"For either named VNL5090N3-E or SKU-selected VNL5050N3-E, N3 input is also its control supply. 3.3 V is below the published 3.5 V minimum. It is not evidence that every sample remains off.\"\n  },\n  \"CAN2_carrier\": {\n    \"native_direct_resistors\": [\n      {\n        \"ref\": \"R36\",\n        \"ohm\": 120,\n        \"dnp\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"ref\": \"R37\",\n        \"ohm\": 120,\n        \"dnp\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"populated_local_termination_conductance_S\": 0,\n    \"TJA1051_differential_input_ohm\": {\n      \"min\": 19000,\n      \"typ\": 30000,\n      \"max\": 52000\n    },\n    \"two_TJA1051_parallel_typ_ohm\": 15000,\n    \"interpretation\": \"Semiconductor input resistance is not a 120-ohm termination. Host module and harness termination are unknown. No frequency-domain or transmission-line conclusion is made.\"\n  }\n}# Polygonus - FOME ECU Module\n\nThis is an ECU \"brain module\". Combined with a \"base board\", it forms a functional engine control unit compatible with [FOME](https://github.com/fome-tech/fome-fw) firmware. It is not intended to run an engine without being mated to a base board.\n\nThis module is a derivative of the [Proteus ECU](https://github.com/mck1117/proteus): for the most part, it is a Proteus with the AMPSEAL connectors replaced with 0.1\" headers. It is 100% firmware compatible with Proteus, and indeed uses the Proteus FOME firmware build.\n\n# Features\n\n## Microcontroller\n\n- STM32F767Zx\n    - 216 MHz ARM Cortex-M7\n    - 1MB or 2MB flash\n    - 512 KB SRAM\n    - LQFP144 package\n\nSome early units use STM32F429ZG, this makes little functional difference.\n\n## Connectivity\n\n- Dual 1 mbit/s CAN bus\n- USB 2.0 full speed (12 mbit/s). Footprint for USB-B connector in addition to header to mount connector on base board. DO NOT route USB signals to the vehicle harness, it will not work reliably.\n- Micro SD card slot. Supports SD + SDHC using an SPI interface.\n- Debug & programming:\n    - [10-pin, 1.27mm Cortex debug header](http://infocenter.arm.com/help/topic/com.arm.doc.faqs/attached/13634/cortex_debug_connectors.pdf)\n    - [6-pin Tag Connect TC2030](https://www.tag-connect.com/product/tc2030-ctx-nl-stdc14-for-use-with-stm32-processors-with-stlink-v3), use with STLINK-V3/STLINK-V3MINI\n\n## Inputs\n\n- 11x analog voltage inputs (weak pulldown to ground to avoid floating)\n- 4x analog temperature inputs (2.7k pullup resistor to 5v)\n- 8x digital inputs with integrated 2.7k pullup resistor to 5v. Two of these are labeled as VR inputs, but this is for compatibility with Proteus. All 8 use identical hardware on Polygonus.\n    - Directly wire to hall cam/crank sensors\n    - Use with a VR interface on the base board\n    - Use for a digital input (oil pressure switch, driver switches and buttons, etc)\n- 2x knock sensor inputs (AC coupled, 1-15khz bandwidth)\n\n## Outputs\n- 12x 4A low-side drivers, LS1-8 + LS13-16. No freewheel diodes, mount on the base board as required.\n- 8x unassigned direct-to-MCU outputs LS9-12 and IGN9-12. Mount injector/ignition drivers on the base board if you have a V12, or use these for something else.\n- 8x 5v ignition (or general purpose) outputs IGN1-8. 5v push-pull, 100mA DC maximum.\n- 2x direct-to-MCU pins for electronic throttle H-bridges on base board.\n- 4x 12v 3A high-side outputs HS1-4.\n\n## Power Supply\n\n- Full operation from 6-24v supply\n- Limited operation from 4-6v\n- Dual 5v sensor supplies, 150mA each, fully protected\n- Dual protected 12v external sensor supply\n\n# Pinout\n\n## Pin Types\n\n**Lowside**: \n\n\n## Table\n\n| Pin | Signal | Type |\n|-----|--------|------|\n| 1 | Ground | |\n| 2 | Ground | |\n| 3 | 12V_MR | 12v supplied from main relay. Supplies high side outputs. |\n| 4 | LS1 | Lowside output |\n| 5 | LS2 | Lowside output |\n| 6 | LS3 | Lowside output |\n| 7 | LS4 | Lowside output |\n| 8 | LS5 | Lowside output |\n| 9 | LS6 | Lowside output |\n| 10 | LS7 | Lowside output |\n| 11 | LS8 | Lowside output |\n| 12 | IGN12 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 13 | IGN11 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 14 | IGN10 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 15 | IGN9 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 16 | IGN8 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 17 | IGN7 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 18 | IGN6 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 19 | IGN5 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 20 | IGN4 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 21 | IGN3 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 22 | IGN2 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 23 | IGN1 | 5v push-pull output |\n| 24 | LS9 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 25 | LS10 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 26 | LS11 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 27 | LS12 | Passthrough to MCU |\n| 28 | LS13 | Lowside output |\n| 29 | LS14 | Lowside output |\n| 30 | LS15 | Lowside output |\n| 31 | LS16 | Lowside output |\n| 32 | 12V_MR | See pin 3\n| 33 | Ground | |\n| 34 | 12V_PROT | Protected 12v output supplied from 12V_IGN\n| 35 | 12V_PROT | See pin 34\n| 36 | 5V_SENSOR_2 | 5v sensor supply |\n| 37 | 5V_SENSOR_2 | 5v sensor supply |\n| 38 | Reserved | |\n| 39 | Reserved | |\n| 40 | 5V_SENSOR_1 | 5v sensor supply |\n| 41 | 5V_SENSOR_1 | 5v sensor supply |\n| 42 | DIGITAL_6 | Digital input |\n| 43 | DIGITAL_5 | Digital input |\n| 44 | DIGITAL_4 | Digital input |\n| 45 | DIGITAL_3 | Digital input |\n| 46 | DIGITAL_2 | Digital input |\n| 47 | DIGITAL_1 | Digital input |\n| 48 | AT4 | Analog temp input |\n| 49 | AT3 | Analog temp input |\n| 50 | AT2 | Analog temp input |\n| 51 | AT1 | Analog temp input |\n| 52 | AV11 | Analog voltage input |\n| 53 | AV10 | Analog voltage input |\n| 54 | AV9 | Analog voltage input |\n| 55 | AV8 | Analog voltage input |\n| 56 | AV7 | Analog voltage input |\n| 57 | AV6 | Analog voltage input |\n| 58 | AV5 | Analog voltage input |\n| 59 | AV4 | Analog voltage input |\n| 60 | AV3 | Analog voltage input |\n| 61 | AV2 | Analog voltage input |\n| 62 | AV1 | Analog voltage input |\n| 63 | Knock 1 | Knock sense input |\n| 64 | Knock 2 | Knock sense input |\n| 65 | HS1 | High side output |\n| 66 | HS2 | High side output |\n| 67 | HS3 | High side output |\n| 68 | HS4 | High side output |\n| 69 | Ground | |\n| 70 | Ground | |\n| 71 | Ground | |\n| 72 | Ground | |\n| 73 | CAN2+ | CAN bus 2 |\n| 74 | CAN2− | CAN bus 2 |\n| 75 | RC1 | |\n| 76 | RC2 | |\n| 77 | Perm_Live | Permanent 12v supply for backup memory supply |\n| 78 | Scope | |\n| 79 | Reserved | |\n| 80 | Reserved | |\n| 81 | +5V | 5v power output for base board (250mA max)\n| 82 | +3.3V | 3.3v power output for base board (100mA max)\n| 83 | ETB1_PWM |\n| 84 | ETB1_DIS |\n| 85 | ETB1_DIR |\n| 86 | ETB2_PWM |\n| 87 | ETB2_DIS |\n| 88 | ETB2_DIR |\n| 89 | Ground | |\n| 90 | 12V_IGN | Switched ignition switch power. 6-24 volts, reverse polarity protected.\n| 91 | Ground | |\n| 92 | Ground | |\n| 93 | CAN+ | CAN bus 1 |\n| 94 | CAN− | CAN bus 1 |\n| 95 | VR2+ | Digital input |\n| 96 | VR1+ | Digital input |\n| 97 | USB_SHIELD | USB shield |\n| 98 | USB_GND | USB ground |\n| 99 | USB+ | USB data D+ |\n| 100 | USB− | USB data D- |\n| 101 | USB_VBUS | USB VBUS input |\n| 102 | +3V3 | 3.3v power output for base board (100mA max) |\n| 103 | EXT_SPI_CS | SPI bus for base board |\n| 104 | EXT_SPI_SCK | SPI bus for base board |\n| 105 | EXT_SPI_MISO | SPI bus for base board |\n| 106 | EXT_SPI_MOSI | SPI bus for base board |\n| 107 | Ground | |\n\"\"\"Read-only native/connectivity audit; run with python3 audit.py.\"\"\"\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport pcbnew\n\nOUT = Path('/work/experiments')\nROOT = Path('/candidate/project')\ndef digest(p):\n    return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\ndef sexpr(path):\n    stack = []\n    root = None\n    for t in re.findall(r'\"(?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*\"|[()]|[^\\s()]+', path.read_text()):\n        if t == '(':\n            n = []\n            if stack:\n                stack[-1].append(n)\n            else:\n                root = n\n            stack.append(n)\n        elif t == ')':\n            stack.pop()\n        else:\n            stack[-1].append(json.loads(t) if t.startswith('\"') else t)\n    return root\n\ndef children(x, tag):\n    return [y for y in x if isinstance(y, list) and y and y[0] == tag]\n\ndef first(x, tag):\n    return next(iter(children(x, tag)), None)\n\nsources = {}\nfor filename in ['Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch', 'Lowside Adder.kicad_sch',\n                 'wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch', 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch',\n                 'vr_module_poly.kicad_sch', 'etb-9201.kicad_sch']:\n    path = ROOT / filename\n    parsed = sexpr(path)\n    comps = []\n    for s in children(parsed, 'symbol'):\n        props = {p[1]: p[2] for p in children(s, 'property')}\n        if props.get('Reference', '').startswith('#'):\n            continue\n        comps.append({'properties': props, 'dnp': first(s, 'dnp'),\n                      'uuid': first(s, 'uuid'), 'position': first(s, 'at')})\n    sources[filename] = {'sha256': digest(path), 'components': comps}\n\nr = ET.parse(OUT / 'independent-netlist.xml').getroot()\nref = ET.parse('/evidence/work/netlist/design.xml').getroot()\ndef nets(tree):\n    return {n.attrib['name']: sorted(z.attrib['ref']+'.'+z.attrib['pin'] for z in n)\n            for n in tree.find('nets')}\nns = nets(r)\nboard = pcbnew.LoadBoard(str(ROOT / 'Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb'))\npads = {f.GetReference()+'.'+p.GetNumber(): p.GetNetname()\n        for f in board.GetFootprints() for p in f.Pads() if p.GetNumber()}\nmismatch = [[pin,n,pads.get(pin)] for n, pins in ns.items()\n            for pin in pins if pads.get(pin) != n]\nselected = {'R1','R2','RN1','RN2','RN3','RN4','U11','U12','U13','U14',\n            'U16','U17','U18','U19','U20','U21','R36','R37','J2','A1'}\nfp = {}\nfor f in board.GetFootprints():\n    if f.GetReference() in selected:\n        fp[f.GetReference()] = {\n            'value': f.GetValue(), 'footprint': str(f.GetFPID().GetUniStringLibId()),\n            'dnp': f.IsDNP(), 'uuid': str(f.m_Uuid.AsString()),\n            'pads': {p.GetNumber(): p.GetNetname() for p in f.Pads() if p.GetNumber()}}\n\ncomps = {c.attrib['ref']: c for c in r.find('components')}\npin_net = {pin:n for n,pins in ns.items() for pin in pins}\nbridges=[]\nfor name,c in comps.items():\n    if name.startswith('R') and not name.startswith('RN'):\n        a,b = pin_net.get(name+'.1'),pin_net.get(name+'.2')\n        if {a,b} == {'/CAN2+','/CAN2-'}:\n            bridges.append({'ref':name,'value':c.findtext('value'),\n                            'dnp':any(p.attrib['name']=='dnp' for p in c.findall('property'))})\n\nresult = {\n    'commands': ['kicad-cli sch export netlist --format kicadxml -o /work/experiments/independent-netlist.xml /candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch',\n                 'python3 /work/experiments/audit.py'],\n    'kicad_version':pcbnew.Version(), 'board_sha256':digest(ROOT/'Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb'),\n    'alias_byte_identical':(ROOT/'VR conditioner.kicad_sch').read_bytes()==(ROOT/'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch').read_bytes(),\n    'sheet_instances':len(r.find('design').findall('sheet')),\n    'component_count':len(comps),'net_count':len(ns),\n    'reference_netlist_identical':ns==nets(ref), 'native_board_pad_net_mismatches':mismatch,\n    'selected_board_footprints':fp,\n    'can2_direct_resistors':bridges,\n    'selected_nets':{n:pins for n,pins in ns.items() if n in ['/LS9','/LS10','/LS11','/LS12',\n        '/IGN9','/IGN10','/IGN11','/IGN12','/CAN2+','/CAN2-','/CAN_TX','/CAN_RX','/CAN_TX2','/CAN_RX2',\n        'Net-(RN2-R4.2)','Net-(RN2-R3.2)']},\n    'native_sources':sources,\n    'limitations':['Pad net identity is not a physical continuity or waveform measurement.',\n                  'No PCB edits, zone refill or candidate modifications.',\n                  'Modules J2, U1, U2 and A1 are treated as interfaces, not flattened circuits.']}\n(OUT/'audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps({k:result[k] for k in ['board_sha256','alias_byte_identical','sheet_instances',\n    'component_count','net_count','reference_netlist_identical','native_board_pad_net_mismatches','can2_direct_resistors']},indent=2))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
