{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"69119fab9d25319b3bf376eca634b13104ba76b7417416b85a2a64a4e78a6ab4\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"accepted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"sheets[0].violations[0:5]; complete report: 5 errors, 348 warnings\",\n          \"path\": \"work/erc/erc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"erc_sheets_equal = true\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/verification.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"check/erc\",\n      \"reason\": \"The declared ERC criterion fails. Independent execution reproduces all 353 violations, including five errors. These establish native rule/model-intent defects, without independently proving missing physical supplies or shorted regulators. Successful execution is not a pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"accepted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[94:97], violations[132:142], schematic_parity and unconnected_items\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Independent violations, schematic_parity and unconnected_items equal fresh evidence\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/verification.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"check/drc\",\n      \"reason\": \"The declared DRC criterion fails. Independent execution reproduces 142 violations and 114 parity issues, including 13 excluded error-level violations. Exclusions and zero unconnected items do not resolve the failing geometric rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"noted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Value VNL5090 and LCSC C2680415 at lines 2549/2583; corresponding repeated symbols and instances\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Lowside Adder.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"board_footprints.U11-U14/U16-U19.properties\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"LCSC product page lines 1222-1227: MPN VNL5050N3TR-E, stock code C2680415\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/source-details.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"circuit/circuit-001\",\n      \"reason\": \"The identity inconsistency is confirmed: all eight switches specify VNL5090 while [LCSC identifies C2680415 as VNL5050N3TR-E](https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2680415.html). Retain it as a minor identification concern. No declared procurement-field consistency criterion or demonstrated electrical incompatibility establishes a defect under the supplied criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"RN1/RN2 pulldown and series networks; second instance RN3/RN4; switch inputs\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Lowside Adder.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"selected_nets, board_footprints and calculations with conditional assumptions\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"ST VNL5090 Tables 6/8; Polygonus README direct-to-MCU outputs\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/source-details.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"ST VNL5050 Tables 6/8: N3 input/supply voltage bounds\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/source-extra.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"circuit/circuit-002\",\n      \"reason\": \"The conditional mechanism is supported: native series drive from a 3.3 V GPIO cannot guarantee the N3 input/supply's 3.5 V minimum, supported by both [VNL5090](https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/vnl5090n3-e.pdf) and [VNL5050](https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/vnl5050s5-e.pdf) specifications. Actual mated-module GPIO levels and reset behavior remain unspecified. The unloaded 2.5 V bias does not predict switch state. Preserve this major compatibility uncertainty pending actual module-drive evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Resistor UUID d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: 120 ohms, DNP yes, R36/R37 instances\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"R36 UUID 6924b9c0-bd5f-481d-9f8d-7fc20978c5ab and R37 UUID 7f8c8af6-f455-43aa-9bef-892e252a308e: DNP attributes\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-: J2.73/74, J1.15/11, U20/U21 and R36/R37\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/connectivity.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"NXP TJA1051 Table 7, differential input resistance 19-52 kohms\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/source-extra.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"circuit/circuit-003\",\n      \"reason\": \"Both native carrier shunts are DNP, leaving no populated resistive carrier termination. The [TJA1051 input resistance](https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/TJA1051.pdf) is not equivalent termination. However, module/harness loading remains unspecified, and neither a standalone-carrier termination requirement nor assembled-bus failure is established. Preserve the major uncertainty pending the actual termination configuration and operating evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"accepted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"lines 21686-21725: five unnumbered thru_hole pads\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"board.design_settings.rules.min_via_annular_width = 0.1; associated drc_exclusions\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pro\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[132:142]: five padstack and five annular_width errors\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"T10 and T12 emit the five specified J1 holes\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/drills/Polygonus-Universal-Base-PTH.drl\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"physical/physical-001\",\n      \"reason\": \"Established native padstack/annular-rule defect: all five plated J1 holes have equal pad and drill diameters, giving zero annulus against the configured 0.1 mm minimum. Independent DRC and plated drill export confirm the condition. Exclusions do not resolve it; connector-fit failure and fabrication rejection remain unproven.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"accepted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"board.design_settings.rules.min_resolved_spokes = 2; exclusions at lines 263-273\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pro\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Saved GND zone UUID bc540b8b-3ffa-4b00-b211-3a91191a1f6d and C15.2/U7.4/C14.2 pads\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[94:97]: starved_thermal, minimum 2, actual 1\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"drc.violations = true\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/verification.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"physical/physical-002\",\n      \"reason\": \"Established saved-copper rule defect: each specified pad resolves one thermal spoke against the configured minimum of two. Independent DRC reproduces all three. Exclusions do not alter copper or resolve the criterion. Routed ground connections limit the conclusion to the spoke-rule violation; no open ground or thermal failure is established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": \"circuit/circuit-003\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"components.R36/R37 and nets /CAN2+, /CAN2-\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/connectivity.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"can2_direct_resistors and board_footprints.R36/R37\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"physical/physical-003\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same DNP termination population and unknown module/harness loading as circuit/circuit-003. Its supported observation and unresolved assembled-bus implications survive in that canonical deferred concern.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"run_id\": \"bafd7961-39b9-4a34-9b39-b7f108e82f07\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.decisions/1\"\n}"}}
